---
/**
 * The first screen's call to action, below the numbers.
 *
 * Its own component because it has to sit *after* the stats strip in the
 * document, and the strip is a sibling of the hero rather than part of it. The
 * order is the argument: introduction, then evidence, then the invitation —
 * asking someone to look at the work before showing them any reason to is the
 * wrong way round.
 *
 * It carries one control, not two. The résumé used to sit beside it; there are
 * now résumé buttons in the header and in the hero's link row, and a third
 * copy of the same link 200px below the second is noise rather than emphasis.
 * `.action` lives in base.css because the hero uses it too.
 */
---

<p class="actions">
  <a class="action action--primary" href="#work">See my works</a>
</p>

<style>
  .actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: var(--s-3);
    margin: 0;
    /* base.css caps every p and li at --measure (64ch) because they are
       normally prose. This one is a control, not a sentence: left capped it
       sat in a 646px box pinned to the left gutter, so `justify-content:
       center` was centring it inside that box rather than on the page. */
    max-width: none;
    width: 100%;
    /* This is the last element on the first screen, so its bottom padding
       is the difference between the button clearing the fold and hanging off
       it. Trimmed to what the fold budget actually allows. */
    padding-bottom: clamp(.5rem, 1.3vh, 1.5rem);
  }
</style>
